module test.claim.review_sheet_header_init_witness

// THE FORMULA-PRESERVING EMPTINESS CARRIER AND THE HEADER-INIT PLANNER, EXERCISED.
//
// TWO KINDS OF CLAIM, AND WHICH IS WHICH. The mint, gunbc.review_sheet_formula_observation
// observe_formula_whole_tab, performs a values.get, and the hermetic frame answers that call with
// the fixture extdeps.google.sheets hermetic_get_values_value_range: an EMPTY whole tab named
// hermetic_get_values_tab. So the mint is EXECUTED here, end to end, for the arms that fixture
// can reach -- an empty tab observed; the request-shape refusals, which fire before the read; and
// the returned-tab mismatch, by asking for a tab the fixture does not answer with. One fixture is
// one response, so the arms that need a DIFFERENT response -- a COLUMNS-major grid, an
// unrecognised majorDimension, an unreadable exchange, an unqualified or malformed returned range,
// and every occupied grid -- are established against formula_grid_admit with the reading SUPPLIED
// (DESIGN 3: a witness discriminates at one interface). The pairing obligation is discharged by
// the executed route: the mint reaches formula_grid_admit with the real read, and plan_header_init
// receives the real carrier.
//
// WHY EMPTINESS IS CLAIMED AT formula_grid_admit AND NOT AT THE PLANNER. Mutation M14 of
// gunbc#11769 (planner ignores the grid) SURVIVED the first cut of this witness: the planner's
// input was sealed, so no claim could hand it an occupied observation. Emptiness now lives in the
// observation module's mint, the carrier exists only for an empty tab, and the occupied reading
// is an unsealed located arm -- which is exactly what lets the planner's occupied arm be executed
// here with a supplied reading (an_occupied_reading_is_planned_as_occupied_never_as_a_write).
//
// WHAT THE FIXTURE CANNOT SHOW, said plainly: that the mint passed FORMULA rather than
// FORMATTED_VALUE to the wire. mock_response ignores its input. formula_whole_tab_render_option
// is the value the mint passes and is asserted here; a mutation that bypasses it at the call site
// is invisible to every hermetic claim and is recorded as such in the PR's mutation table.

